  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = -2x^{2} + 16x - 5\\). What is the maximum value of \\(f(x)\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "27"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The maximum occurs at \\(x = -\\frac{b}{2a} = -\\frac{16}{2(-2)} = 4\\).",
    "\\(f(4) = -2(16) + 16(4) - 5 = -32 + 64 - 5 = 27\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nf = -2*x**2 + 16*x - 5\nxv = solve(diff(f, x), x)[0]\nassert xv == 4 and f.subs(x, xv) == 27\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [f.subs(x, xv)]",
